# Daily Tour — Code Owners
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Syntax (one rule per line; later rules override earlier ones for the same path):
#   <path-glob>   @user1 @user2 @org/team
#
# As the team grows, add per-directory rules above the global catch-all, e.g.:
#   /apps/pwa/        @zmeireles @frontend-team
#   /services/bff/    @zmeireles @backend-team
#   /docs/            @zmeireles @docs-team
#   /infra/           @zmeireles @devops-team
#
# A user must have write access to the repo to be a valid code owner.

# Global owner — required reviewer for every PR until per-area owners are set.
*   @zmeireles
